{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Blender mathutils Vector Method Dispatch.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Blender mathutils Vector Method Dispatch.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"blender mathutils vector method dispatch blender mathutils vector method dispatch","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Blender mathutils Vector Method Dispatch.md","fileName":"Blender mathutils Vector Method Dispatch.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Blender mathutils Vector Method Dispatch","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-14 00:20\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Blender Embedded Python Internals]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Blender Embedded Python Internals","Blender Python Method Table","Blender mathutils Extension","Blender BLI API","coreblenderdevelopment.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Blender mathutils Vector Method Dispatch.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Blender mathutils Vector Method Dispatch.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"blender mathutils vector method dispatch blender mathutils vector method dispatch","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Blender mathutils Vector Method Dispatch.md","fileName":"Blender mathutils Vector Method Dispatch.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Blender mathutils Vector Method Dispatch","heading":"Blender mathutils Vector Method Dispatch","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"When a script calls a `mathutils.Vector` method, CPython uses the type's [[Blender Python Method Table]] to invoke the registered C function. The normalization method, for example, obtains the vector data, checks callback access, calls blenlib's normalization routine, reports any write callback, and returns Python's `None`.\n\nThe same table can expose class methods, methods that mutate the original object, methods that return copies, and operations involving another value. This dispatch keeps the public Python class concise while reusing implementations from the [[Blender mathutils Extension]] and [[Blender BLI API]].","tags":["baby"],"links":["Blender Embedded Python Internals","Blender Python Method Table","Blender mathutils Extension","Blender BLI API","coreblenderdevelopment.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Blender mathutils Vector Method Dispatch.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Blender mathutils Vector Method Dispatch.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"blender mathutils vector method dispatch blender mathutils vector method dispatch","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Blender mathutils Vector Method Dispatch.md","fileName":"Blender mathutils Vector Method Dispatch.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Blender mathutils Vector Method Dispatch","heading":"References","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"[[coreblenderdevelopment.pdf]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Blender Embedded Python Internals","Blender Python Method Table","Blender mathutils Extension","Blender BLI API","coreblenderdevelopment.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""}]}